#* {{quote-book|en|title=w:Valley of the Dolls|page=214|author=w:Jacqueline Susann|year=1966|passage=That's long enough for any small town." Lyon leaned forward. "Do you like Lawrenceville, Mr. Hill?" The driver cocked his head. "Aeah. Why not? Born here. It's a '''right''' nice town|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=FMSUrZYIYF0C&pg=PA214&dq=%22right+kind%7Cnice%22+town%7Cfarm%7Ctree%7Cforest%7Cfield%7Cvillage++-%22the+right+kind%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=EllfT4mBPKHo0QGzwdGLBw&ved=0CM4BEOgBMBs#v=onepage&q=%22right%20kind%7Cnice%22%20town%7Cfarm%7Ctree%7Cforest%7Cfield%7Cvillage%20%20-%22the%20right%20kind%22&f=false}}<!--Aeah => Maine or, at least, New England. Context is Massachusetts)) -->
