# {{senseid|en|affirming agreement}} Yes, that is [[correct]]; I [[agree]].
#* {{quote-text|en|date=March 6 2007|author=w:Julie Rutterford|title=[[:w:Life_on_Mars_(British_TV_series)|Life on Mars]]|section=[[:w:List_of_Life_on_Mars_(British_TV_series)_episodes|Season 2, Episode 3]]
|passage=''Sam Tyler:'' Look, look, you know when I said I wasn't wrong? Well, I was. But I was right about this not being the IRA. I was right to follow my instincts. Like you said, go with your gut feeling. I'm just taking your lead.<br>''Gene Hunt:'' So I'm right.<br>''Sam Tyler:'' We both are.<br>''Gene Hunt:'' Right.<br>''Sam Tyler:'' '''Right'''.<br>''Gene Hunt:'' Just [[as long as]] I'm more right than you.}}
#* '''2016''', [https://web.archive.org/web/20181113034859/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/lets-learn-english-lesson-2-hello/3113733.html VOA Learning English] (public domain)
#*: Tell her you’re here.<br>'''Right'''. Thanks, Pete.
#: {{ux|en|— United's the best team in the country.<br/>— '''Right'''. And they'll go all the way for sure.<br/>— Damn '''right''' they will.}}
# {{senseid|en|acknowledging the other's utterance, independently of agreement}} I have listened to what you just said and I acknowledge your assertion or opinion, regardless of whether I agree with it (opinion) or can verify it (assertion).
#* {{quote-text|en|date=March 6 2007|author=w:Julie Rutterford|title=[[:w:Life_on_Mars_(British_TV_series)|Life on Mars]]|section=[[:w:List_of_Life_on_Mars_(British_TV_series)_episodes|Season 2, Episode 3]]
|passage=''Sam Tyler:'' Look, look, you know when I said I wasn't wrong? Well, I was. But I was right about this not being the IRA. I was right to follow my instincts. Like you said, go with your gut feeling. I'm just taking your lead.<br>''Gene Hunt:'' So I'm right.<br>''Sam Tyler:'' We both are.<br>''Gene Hunt:'' '''Right'''.<br>''Sam Tyler:'' Right.<br>''Gene Hunt:'' Just [[as long as]] I'm more right than you.}}
#: {{ux|en|— United's the best team in the country, so they'll come up with something.<br/>— '''Right'''. And do you think they'll go all the way?}}
# {{senseid|en|signpost marking change of subject}} {{non-gloss|[[signpost|Signpost]] word to change the subject in a [[discussion]] or [[discourse]]}}.
#: {{ux|en|— After that interview, I don't think we should hire her.<br/>— '''Right'''. Who wants lunch?}}
# {{senseid|en|checking engagement and agreement}} {{non-gloss|Used to check listener engagement and (especially) agreement at the end of an utterance or each segment thereof}}.
#: {{ux|en|You're going, '''right'''?}}
#: {{ux|en|I went downstairs, '''right''', and I was going to call her, but I found this note, '''right''', so what am I supposed to do now?}}
# {{non-gloss|Used to add seriousness or decisiveness before a statement.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1987|title=w:Withnail and I
|passage=<span style="font-variant:small-caps">Withnail:</span> '''Right''' {{...}} I'm gonna do the washing up.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The {{l|en|polysemy|polysemic}} ambiguity, regarding the senses of (1) affirming agreement and (2) acknowledging an utterance independently of agreement, sometimes functions {{l|en|polite|politely}} as a {{w|social lubricant}}, avoiding any {{l|en|sarcasm|sarcastic}} connotation that {{m|en|OK}} might easily imply; the degree of clarity is sufficient in contexts where getting to the bottom of who agrees or disagrees is superfluous to the purpose of the conversation.

