===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:regretten<ety:bor<fro:regreter<ety:af<re-><*greter<ety:der<frk:*grātan>>>>>>|tree=1}}

From {{inh|en|enm|regretten}}, {{m|enm|regreten}}, from {{der|en|fro|regreter}}, {{m|fro|regrater|t=to lament}}, from {{m|fro|re-|pos=intensive prefix}} + {{m|fro|*greter}}, {{m|fro|*grater|t=to weep}}, from {{der|en|frk|*grātan|t=to weep, mourn, lament}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*grētaną|t=to weep}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰreh₁d-|t=to sound}}; and {{der|en|frk|*greutan|t=to cry, weep}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*greutaną|t=to weep, cry}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gʰrewd-|t=to weep, be sad}}, equivalent to {{af|en|re-|greet}}. Cognate with {{cog|goh|grāzan|t=to cry}}, {{cog|ang|grǣtan|t=to weep, greet}}, {{cog|ang|grēotan|t=to weep, lament}}, {{cog|non|gráta|t=to weep, groan}}, {{cog|got|𐌲𐍂𐌴𐍄𐌰𐌽|t=to weep}}. More at {{m|en|greet}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈɡɹɛt/|/ɹəˈɡɹɛt/|/ɹiˈɡɹɛt/}}
