===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=relief|:inh|enm:reste|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|rest}}, {{m|enm|reste}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ræst}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*rastu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*rastō}}, of uncertain origin; possibly derived from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₁reh₁-|t=to rest}} or {{m|ine-pro|*Hre(h₁)s-|t=to flow, rush}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|rêst|t=rest}}, {{cog|nl|rust|t=rest}}, {{cog|de|Rast|t=rest}}, {{cog|sv|rast|t=rest}}, {{cog|no|rest|t=rest}}, {{cog|is|röst|t=rest}}, {{cog|sga|árus|t=dwelling}}, {{cog|de|Ruhe|t=calm}}, {{cog|sq|resht|t=to stop, pause}}, {{cog|cy|araf|t=quiet, calm, gentle}}, {{cog|lt|rovà|t=calm}}, {{cog|grc|ἐρωή|t=rest, respite}}, {{cog|ae|𐬀𐬌𐬭𐬌𐬨𐬈|t=calm, peaceful}}, {{cog|sa|रमते|tr=rámate|t=he stays still, calms down}}, {{cog|got|𐍂𐌹𐌼𐌹𐍃|t=tranquility}}. Related to {{l|en|roo}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{topics|en|Sleep}} {{lb|en|uncountable|of a [[person]] or [[animal]]}} [[relief|Relief]] from [[work]] or [[activity]] by sleeping; [[sleep]].
#: {{syn|en|sleep|slumber}}
#: {{ux|en|I need to get a good '''rest''' tonight; I was up late last night.}}
#: {{ux|en|The sun sets, and the workers go to their '''rest'''.}}
# {{topics|en|Rest}} {{lb|en|countable}} Any relief from [[exertion]]; a [[state]] of [[quiet]] and [[relaxation]].
#: {{syn|en|break|repose|time off}}
#: {{ux|en|We took a '''rest''' at the top of the hill to get our breath back.}}
# {{topics|en|Peace}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[peace|Peace]]; [[freedom]] from [[worry]], [[anxiety]], [[annoyance]]s; [[tranquility]].
#: {{syn|en|peace|quiet|roo|silence|stillness|tranquility}}
#: {{ux|en|It was nice to have a '''rest''' from the phone ringing when I unplugged it for a while.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Judges|3|30|passage=And the land had '''rest''' fourscore years.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|of an [[object]] or [[concept]]}} A state of [[inactivity]]; a state of little or no [[motion]]; a state of [[completion]].
#: {{ux|en|The boulder came to '''rest''' just behind the house after rolling down the mountain.}}
#: {{ux|en|The ocean was finally at '''rest'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Now that we're all in agreement, we can put that issue to '''rest'''.}}
# {{lb|en|euphemistic|uncountable}} A [[final]] [[position]] after [[death]]. Also, death itself: "Not alone, not alone would I go to my rest in the heart of the love..." -- George William Russell ("Love")
#: {{syn|en|peace}}
#: {{ux|en|She was laid to '''rest''' in the village cemetery.}}
# {{topics|en|Silence}} {{senseid|en|music}} {{lb|en|music|countable}} A [[pause]] of a specified length in a piece of music.
#: {{hypo|en|breve rest|demisemiquaver rest|hemidemisemiquaver rest|minim rest|quaver rest|semibreve rest|semiquaver rest}}
#: {{ux|en|Remember there's a '''rest''' at the end of the fourth bar.}}
# {{lb|en|music|countable}} A [[written]] [[symbol]] indicating such a pause in a musical [[score]] such as in [[sheet music]].
# {{senseid|en|no motion}}{{lb|en|physics|uncountable}} [[absence|Absence]] of [[motion]].
#: {{ant|en|motion}}
#: {{ux|en|The body's centre of gravity may affect its state of '''rest'''.}}
# {{lb|en|snooker|countable}} A stick with a U-, V- or X-shaped head used to support the tip of a [[cue]] when the [[cue ball]] is otherwise out of reach.
#: {{hyper|en|bridge}}
#: {{ux|en|Higgins can't quite reach the white with his cue, so he'll be using the '''rest'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Any object [[design]]ed to be used to support something else.
#: {{syn|en|cradle|q1=of a telephone|support}}
#: {{ux|en|She put the phone receiver back in its '''rest'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|He placed his hands on the arm '''rests''' of the chair.}}
#: {{hypo|en|arm rest|elbow rest|foot rest|head rest|leg rest|neck rest|wrist rest}}
# {{topics|en|Armor}} A [[projection]] from the right side of the [[cuirass]] of [[armour]], serving to support the [[lance]].
#* {{RQ:Dryden Fables|The Flower and the Leaf
|passage=their visors closed, their lances in the '''rest'''}}
# A place where one may rest, either temporarily, as in an inn, or permanently, as, in an abode.
#* '''c. 1851''', Catholicus (pen name of {{w|John Henry Newman}}, ''letter in The Times''
#*: halfway houses and travellers' '''rests'''
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=9|passage=in dust our final '''rest''', and native home|year=1873}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Deuteronomy|xii|9|passage=Ye are not as yet come to the '''rest''' and to the inheritance which the Lord your God giveth you.}}
# {{lb|en|poetry}} A short pause in reading poetry; a [[caesura]].
# The striking of a balance at regular intervals in a running account. Often, specifically, the intervals after which compound interest is added to capital.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1874|author=New York Court of Appeals|journal=Records and Briefs
|passage=a new account was opened under the heading "Irondale Mine" and so continued witli '''semiannual''' rest}}
# {{topics|en|Games}} {{lb|en|dated}} A [[set]] or [[game]] at [[tennis]].

