===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|resten}}, from {{inh|en|ang|restan}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*rastijan|t=to rest}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ros-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*res-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*erH-|t=rest}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|rusten|t=to rest}}, {{cog|gml|resten|t=to rest}}, {{cog|de|rasten|t=to rest}}, {{cog|da|raste|t=to rest}}, {{cog|sv|rasta|t=to rest}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[cease]] from action, motion, work, or performance of any kind; [[stop]]; [[desist]]; be without motion.
#: {{ux|en|My day's work is over; now I will '''rest'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I shall not '''rest''' until I have uncovered the truth.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Exodus|23|12|passage=Six days thou shalt do thy work, and on the seventh day thou shalt '''rest'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=July 8, 1876|author=Christopher E. Benck| title=Recipes for traditional English foods| passage=After the sugar beets are strained, pour in a large amount of honey and let it '''rest''' for thirty minutes. This will form the base for our delicious honey tender.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To come to a [[pause]] or an end; [[end]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be free from that which harasses or disturbs; be quiet or still; be undisturbed.
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=1|passage=There '''rest''', if any rest can harbour there.|year=1873}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|reflexive|copulative}} To put into a state of rest.
#: {{ux|en|We need to '''rest''' the horses before we ride any further.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1485|author=Sir {{w|Thomas Malory}}|title=w:Le Morte d'Arthur|section=Book X
|passage=And thereby at a pryory they '''rested''' them all nyght.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=September 29, 2011|author=Jon Smith|work=BBC Sport| title=[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/15014632.stm Tottenham 3-1 Shamrock Rovers]| passage=With the north London derby to come at the weekend, Spurs boss Harry Redknapp opted to '''rest''' many of his key players, although he brought back Aaron Lennon after a month out through injury.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[stay]], [[remain]], be situated, or belong to.
#: {{ux|en|The blame seems to '''rest''' with your father.}}
#: {{ux|en|Copyright in the typographical arrangement '''rests''' with the Crown.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[rely]] or [[depend]] on.
#: {{ux|en|The decision [[rest on|'''rests''' on]] getting a bank loan.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be [[based on]]; to rely on something for proof or explanation
#: {{syn|en|[[repose]] (formal)}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1700|author=w:John Dryden|title=Sigismonda and Guiscardo
|passage=On him I '''rested''', after long debate, / And not without considering, fixed fate.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-08-03|volume=408|issue=8847|magazine=w:The Economist| title=[http://www.economist.com/news/finance-and-economics/21582498-america-has-changed-way-it-measures-gdp-boundary-problems Boundary problems]| passage=Economics is a messy discipline: too fluid to be a science, too rigorous to be an art. Perhaps it is fitting that economists’ most-used metric, gross domestic product (GDP), is a tangle too.{{...}}But as a foundation for analysis it is highly subjective: it '''rests''' on difficult decisions about what counts as a territory, what counts as output and how to value it. Indeed, economists are still tweaking it.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive|reflexive}} To [[lean]], [[lie]], or [[lay]].
#: {{ux|en|A column '''rests''' on its pedestal.}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''rested''' my head in my hands.}}
#: {{ux|en|She '''rested''' against my shoulder.}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''rested''' against the wall for a minute.}}
# {{lb|en|US|_|law|ambitransitive}} To complete one's active [[advocacy]] in a [[trial]] or other [[proceeding]], and thus to wait for the [[outcome]] (however, one is still generally available to answer questions, etc.)
#: {{ux|en|The defense '''rests''', your Honor.}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''rest''' my case.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[sleep]]; [[slumber]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To lie [[dormant]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To sleep the final sleep; sleep in [[death]]; [[die]]; be dead.
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XXI|35|I sing to him that '''rests''' below,<br>⁠And, since the grasses round me wave,<br>⁠I take the grasses of the grave,<br>And make them pipes whereon to blow.}}
# To be satisfied; to acquiesce.
#* {{RQ:Addison Cato|19|passage=to '''rest''' in Heaven's determination}}

