|chapter=4|title=[http://openlibrary.org/works/OL16814587W Pulling the Strings]
|passage=Soon after the arrival of Mrs. Campbell, dinner was announced by Abboye. He came into the drawing room '''resplendent''' in his gold-and-white turban. […] His cummerbund matched the turban in gold lines.}}
