====Usage notes====
* Often used in formal or literary contexts to convey exceptional brilliance or magnificence, whether literal (visual splendor) or figurative (outstanding achievement, noble character, etc.).
* Commonly paired with prepositions {{m|en|in}} (resplendent in robes) or {{m|en|with}} (resplendent with jewels).

